from ../structure import StructuralContext

export abstract anchor SourceRecord:
    file:: string
    line:: number
    entity:: string
    propertyPath:: string
    text:: string
    rules:: string[]
    inputs:: string[]

export anchor Provenance:
    description:
        Every result analysis produces can be traced back to the words or
        structure it came from. This is not a convenience. If an
        implementation turns out to be wrong because a requirement was wrong,
        the requirement has to lead back to the sentence that said it, so the
        sentence can be fixed.

    whatIsRecorded:
        Each fact carries a source record, whose shape is the SourceRecord
        anchor below.

        ```text
        file          where it was written               button.pi
        line          the line its statement starts on   9
        entity        the entity it belongs to           Button
        propertyPath  the property it was written in     Button.disabled
        text          the original words, unchanged      It cannot be clicked.
        rules         every rule applied, in order       scope condition, capability pattern
        inputs        facts it was derived from          (none)
        ```

        A structural fact records the declaration it was read from. A derived
        fact has no text of its own; its inputs name the facts it came from,
        and each of those has its own record, so a derived fact can always be
        followed back to source text in a finite number of steps.

    neverLost:
        Normalization changes how a fact is written, never where it came from.
        The text in a source record is the original text, not a cleaned up
        version, and it is kept even when the fact that came from it is
        partial or was never produced at all.

    bothDirections:
        Tracing works both ways. From a fact, the source record leads to the
        text. From any statement, analysis can list every fact, condition and
        open item that came from it, including when the answer is none.

    example:
        ```text
        when Button.state = disabled: Button cannot be clicked
          id        button.pi#Button.disabled/s3/f1
          file      button.pi, line 9
          property  Button.disabled
          text      It cannot be clicked.
          rules     statement split, pronoun it -> Button,
                    scope condition disabled -> Button.state = disabled,
                    capability pattern
        ```

        The structure that made disabled a condition is described in
        @{StructuralContext}.
